maludb-os-core (2026.11.09maluos2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * A sign-in over plain http works: vendored at the kernel's branch
    fix/http-session-cookie (9aad43f, main 9e931ca and one commit). With
    APP_ENV=prod the session cookie was always Secure, so an office served
    over http (scheme: http, a LAN without a TLS proxy) never got its session
    back from the browser and every sign-in failed the CSRF check, whatever
    the password. To be re-vendored at main once the pull request is merged.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 23:55:00 +0000

